"Man dies in leopard attack in Mandi, 5 others injured; animal succumbs after villagers retaliate - The Indian Express",2025-12-24,Himachal Pradesh,Mandi,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,5.0,1.0,"A man died in a leopard attack in Mandi, and 5 others were injured.",0.98,single_incident,,The Indian Express,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Man dies in leopard attack in Mandi, 5 others injured; animal succumbs after villagers retaliate
The leopard first targeted residents of Chandiyal in Mandi before entering Bhadyal, where four people were seriously injured in separate attacks. It then attacked Balbir Singh in Malwana, killing him.
A man was killed and five others, including two women, were injured after a leopard attacked them around 7 am in Himachal Pradesh’s Mandi district Wednesday morning. The leopard was later attacked by villagers and succumbed to the injuries.
Forest officials identified the victim as Balbir Singh, 39, who had come to Malwana village to visit relatives. The injured have been identified as Sahib Singh, Deena Nath, Champa Devi, Janit, and Rekha Devi. They were admitted to Shri Lal Bahadur Shastri Medical College in Nerchowk.
Preliminary findings suggest that Balbir had stepped out to relieve himself when the leopard attacked him. The injured belonged to three different villages in the Balh Valley. The animal first targeted residents of Chandiyal village before entering Bhadyal, where four people were seriously injured in separate attacks. It later attacked Balbir in Malwana village, killing him on the spot.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1213 chars)"
Maharashtra: Leopard mauls 10-year-old to death; body found 1.5 km away from spot of attack - Times Now,2020-11-28,,,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,A leopard mauled a 10-year-old to death.,0.5,single_incident,,Times Now,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Aurangabad: In yet another incident of human-wildlife conflict, a leopard attacked and killed a 10-year-old boy at a village in Beed district of Maharashtra on Friday. The body of the victim was found more than 1 km away from the spot of the attack.
The incident took place at Kinhi village in the district’s Ashti taluka on Friday afternoon. The now-deceased boy, identified as Sarthak Bankar, was attacked by the leopard when he was on a farm. Farmers who were working in nearby fields rushed to save him after hearing his cries for help, but in vain as the big cat had dragged him away.
Boy's dead body found in bushes
“The farmers found the boy’s body in the bushes, at a distance of about 1.5 km, after a two-hour search with wounds on the neck and some other parts of the body,” a report by The Times of India quoted forest officials as saying.
Responding to a question, forest range officer Amol Munde it was too early to declare the leopard a man-eater. A combing operation in the area is underway. Sources told TOI that the local police and forest officials are planning to track the big cat with the help of drone cameras.
Similar incident
A 40-year-old farmer, identified as Nagnath Garje, was mauled to death by a leopard in a neighbour village three days ago.
The leopard killed Garje when he was working on his field in Surdi village on Tuesday. When he didn’t return home after work, a search was carried out in the area and he was found dead.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1458 chars)"
Water pipeline worker attacked by leopard in Himachal Pradesh - Indiablooms,2020-12-24,Himachal Pradesh,,Leopard,Human Injury,0.0,1.0,0.0,Water pipeline worker attacked by leopard.,0.98,single_incident,,Indiablooms,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxQcVM4ME9RWWJkSzVmaWZKTS1BTk80UjFxa2tNSjVsSnpVaDNsOWoxUEZqNlliM3RHWUJxdzA1YjJfSUhJX1FULXVURGplY2ZoczBhVEJnbGV4SE85YW4ySzVtZEV6VFMwN1JKa0FlbnJ6SFJhQTVjbkkwX0JrT2dHSnFDeW0yY2RWeG5HUVdINDhOdXJQWWxiaTg2LWFEcXhLMXkyeGRNSQ?oc=5,,,"Water pipeline worker attacked by leopard in Himachal Pradesh
Shimla/UNI: A 45-year-old man working in a forest near Shimla was injured after being attacked by a leopard, police said on Thursday.
The leopard, who reportedly attacked the man while he was laying a water pipeline, fled the spot when the victim's co-workers arrived on hearing his cries.
According to police, the incident occurred in the forest adjoining Salana village near Shoghi at about 1530 hrs on Wednesday afternoon, when some workers were laying water pipelines in the area for an irrigation and public health (IPH) project.
	
“One of them, Abdul Gafur, was allegedly attacked by the leopard while he was at work. The rest of the workers were present some distance away. They rushed to the spot after hearing Gafur's cries and the animal fled on seeing them,” said a police official.
Gafur received injuries on his right leg where the leopard attacked him with its paw, and was given first aid before being rushed to the IGMC hospital in Shimla for treatment, the police said.
	
The victim is a resident of Mandi in Poonch district of Jammu and Kashmir, and had arrived in Shimla along with his two sons and five others after being hired by an IPH contractor, officials said.
“We have alerted the forest authorities, and the concerned divisional forest officer has sent a wildlife team to the spot to search and capture the animal,” he added.
