Man vs leopard: Big cat attacks man; gets killed by irate villagers in front of forest department officials - Times Now,2020-04-12,,,Leopard,Retaliation Against Wildlife,0.0,0.0,0.0,A leopard attacked a man and was killed by villagers.,0.98,single_incident,,Times Now,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi_?oc=5,,,"Lucknow: In yet another incident of man-animal conflict a leopard was allegedly thrashed to death with sticks in a wheat field after it launched an attack on a local near Susundi village in Varanasi division’s Ghazipur district. The big cat, in self-defence, left three people injured when it tried to escape.
Villagers overlook instructions of police and forest officials
Divisional forest officer Ghazipur Girish Chandra Tripathi stated that the officials of the forest department and the local police repeatedly urged the villagers to leave the area and allow them to capture it, but the villagers chose to overlook their instructions and killed the beast. The incident took place within the territorial jurisdiction of the Nonahara Police Station. The accused have been booked under Section 9/51 of the Wildlife Protection Act. Further, he mentioned that the feline’s carcass was sent for conducting a post mortem examination.
Leopard attacks local
According to the Times of India, the strayed leopard attacked a local on Sunday. The victim alerted the villagers about the presence of the beast in the area. After attacking the man, the leopard entered into a wheat field and hid. Hundreds of villagers arrived at the field and encircled it to trap the big cat. Upon receiving information, a police team also arrived at the spot.
Leopard's bid to escape
The DFO said that he also arrived at the wheat field after receiving information from the district collector. Tripathi said that he and the police team repeatedly requested the villagers to leave the area and enable them to capture the big cat. But they refused to listen to them. Then, the angry mob began shouting which scared the beast and it attempted to flee from the field.
While attempting to escape from the mob surrounding the field, the leopard attacked the mob, leaving three people injured. Later, the infuriated mob thrashed the big cat with sticks. It died on the spot.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1941 chars)"
"Leopard mauls down a person to death, injures five in Balh valley of Mandi district - himachalguardian.com",2025-12-24,Himachal Pradesh,Mandi,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,5.0,1.0,Leopard attack resulted in one death and five injuries.,0.98,single_incident,,himachalguardian.com,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxNTC00eHdkTFhSZFdWN1Q3LXc3UGRMem53bFdBMFUtRmRZWWthNnpBTjRFb2IzR3ZROHJOV0tNcGdTTWgxczFZeTVIbHFPaVRfWUhRYTNJU3RqVGZJTEFfQWtrS1YtQmtZZHp1czcyYmUxd1R3aFgwdUlIQURUUVljUW9IZFY1Y21pOEhGc2VVdVEzcHZFZUQ1SktZczVReC1oZlpZcnZvRU02MU40dlhQR0Z1cmJhN1JWOUt0Xw?oc=5,,,"One person was mauled down to death by a leopard and five others injured in Bhadyal and surrounding villages in Balh valley of Mandi district on Wednesday morning creating a scare among people, who later killed the beast.
