Elderly man killed by leopard in Uttarakhand’s Chamoli district | India News - Hindustan Times,2020-12-01,Uttarakhand,Chamoli,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,An elderly man was killed by a leopard.,0.98,single_incident,,Hindustan Times,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Elderly man killed by leopard in Uttarakhand’s Chamoli district
This is not the first such attack to be reported from the state, where human-leopard conflict has been increasing. In the first week of November a 21-year-old woman was killed in a leopard attack in Champawat district.
A 65-year-old man was killed in a leopard attack on Monday in Chamoli district, forest officials said.
The man was attacked by the leopard on his way to the market on Monday morning in Joshimath block of the district.
After the attack, locals present at the spot made a noise due to which the leopard went back to the forest area, but angry locals protested till evening with the deceased’s body on the road.
JS Suhag, chief wildlife warden of the Uttarakhand forest department said, “I have ordered to install cages in the area to try to capture the leopard. This is the second incident of an attack by a leopard from the area. A few days ago a Nepali worker was attacked by a leopard.”
The senior forest official said that the leopard will be declared a man-eater if any further attacks take place.
This is not the first such attack to be reported from the state, where human-leopard conflict has been increasing. In the first week of November a 21-year-old woman was killed in a leopard attack in Champawat district.
Three women, including a teenager lost their lives in a week in October in Okhalkanda block of Nainital.
On October 21, a 13-year-old girl was killed in a leopard attack in Nainital district when she was going to the forest to cut grass. On October 15, an 11-year-old girl was killed by a leopard in Jaspur area in US Nagar district when she was playing with her siblings outside her house.
On October 14, a 40-year-old woman was mauled to death by a leopard in Pithoragarh district when she had gone to the forests to cut grass.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1832 chars)"
"In Uttarakhand’s Pithoragarh, 40-year-old woman killed by leopard | India News - Hindustan Times",2020-10-15,Uttarakhand,Pithoragarh,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,A 40-year-old woman was killed by a leopard.,0.98,single_incident,,Hindustan Times,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"In Uttarakhand’s Pithoragarh, 40-year-old woman killed by leopard
This is not the first incident of a leopard attack in the state. On October 11, a 7-year-old girl was killed by a leopard in Tehri Garhwal district when she had gone to use the washroom outside her house. This was the fifth case of a child being killed by a leopard in the past one month.
In yet another incident of leopard attack, a 40-year-old woman was mauled to death by a leopard in Pithoragarh district on Wednesday evening when she had gone to the forests to cut grass.
Vinay Bhargav, divisional forest officer of Pithoragarh division said the incident happened around 4 pm on Wednesday in Papdeo Van Panchayat area.
“When the woman had gone to cut grass in the forests, she was mauled by the leopard and the animal further dragged her around 50 metres into dense bushes. Upon hearing her scream, other women who had accompanied her reached the site by tracing the blood trail, but the woman had died by then,” Bhargav said.
The body was recovered by local forest staff and sent to the district hospital for a post-mortem examination.
“As the incident happened inside a forest area, it prima facie appears to be a result of confrontation and panic attack,” said the forest official.
This is not the first incident of a leopard attack in the state. On October 11, a 7-year-old girl was killed by a leopard in Tehri Garhwal district when she had gone to use the washroom outside her house. This was the fifth case of a child being killed by a leopard in the past one month. On October 7, a 7-year-old girl was killed in a leopard attack outside her house in Berinag division of Pithoragarh district. On October 1, a 14-year-old boy was killed in a leopard attack in Pauri Garhwal district when he took his cattle for grazing in the forest area.
On September 24, an 11-year-old girl was killed in a leopard attack in Pithoragarh district when she was working near her house and collecting fodder. On September 19, a 7-year-old girl was mauled to death by a leopard when she was playing near her house in Almora district. On September 22, a 40-year-old man was also killed by a leopard in the Pithoragarh district.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 2183 chars)"
"'Man-eater' leopard attacks woman, tears her stomach apart in Uttarakhand - Times Now",2020-08-09,Uttarakhand,,Leopard,Human Injury,0.0,1.0,0.0,Leopard attacked and injured a woman in Uttarakhand.,0.98,single_incident,,Times Now,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Dehradun: In yet another incident of human-wildlife conflict, a “man-eater” leopard mauled a 35-year-old woman to death in Tehri district of Uttarakhand on Friday night. This is the second incident of death due to a leopard attack in the district in six days. An eight-year-old girl was killed in Pratapnagar block on August 3.
The incident took place in Maletha area of Narendra Nagar forest division at 10 pm on Friday. The now-deceased woman was sitting in the courtyard of her house when the big walked in and pounced on her. She was killed in a brutal manner. Intestines were oozing out of the woman's body as the leopard had torn her stomach apart, a forest official said
Not an accidental killing, says SDO
The victim’s body was sent to Srinagar Medical College Hospital for conducting post-mortem examination. “The attack was not accidental and the leopard has turned into a man-eater. It kept an eye on its prey, attacked it, killed it and then ate it,” a report by The Times of India quoted DP Balooni, SDO, Narendra Nagar Forest Division as saying. The nature of killing is different during accidental human-leopard interactions, the SDO added.
Permission granted to trap leopard
A request was sent to chief wildlife warden JS Suhag to allow either trapping or termination of the leopard with a shooter’s help. Suhag has granted permission to trap the leopard. Balooni said that an initial ex-gratia of Rs 3 lakh has been given to the deceased woman’s kin.
Another incident
Last month, a seven-year-old leopard was shot dead by a team of three sharpshooters after it killed two children in Narayasnbagarh forest range of Chamoli district. The authorities declared the big cat as “dangerous to human life” and began combing operations. It was killed when it visited the spot of its second killing.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1807 chars)"
‘Dangerous to human life’: Leopard shot dead after it killed 2 children in Uttarakhand - Times Now,2020-07-12,Uttarakhand,,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,2.0,Leopard that killed two children was shot dead in Uttarakhand.,0.98,single_incident,,Times Now,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Dehradun: A leopard that had mauled two children to death was shot dead by a team of three shooters and forest department officials in Narayasnbagarh forest range in Uttarakhand’s Chamoli district on Friday. The combing operations began ten days ago after authorities declared the seven-year-old big cat as ‘dangerous to human life’.
The first attack took place in Bhayada Malethi village where the leopard killed a four-year-old boy on May 29. Then, exactly a month later on June 29, it mauled an eleven-year-old girl to death in Gairbam village. The aerial distance between the two villages is just 2 km.
The forest officials identified the big cat with the help its pugmarks. It was shot dead by shooter Joy Hukkil when it revisited the spot of its second kill in Gairbam village on Friday night, Chamoli divisional forest officer Ashutosh Singh told The Times of India.
Third leopard shot dead since January
According to the sources, this is the third leopard that has been shot dead in Uttarakhand since January 2020. A total of six big cats have been declared as ‘dangerous to human life’ in in the state. Meanwhile, combing operations are on for two more leopards in Nainital and Almora that are responsible for killing three people each.
Search on for two more leopards
Sources told TOI that the big cat in Almora is active in Bhasiyachana block. It has mauled three people to death since April. Authorities have issued a ‘red alert’ to the villagers. Shooters from Bijnor and Nainital are tracing the animal.
Meanwhile, in Nainital, the forest officials have obtained permission to either capture or shoot the leopard that killed three people. The plan to deploy shooters is underway besides setting up camera traps and intensive patrolling in the vulnerable areas of the forest zone.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1793 chars)"
Leopard Kills 5-Year-Old Boy In Uttarakhand: Forest Official - NDTV,2022-11-22,Uttarakhand,,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,Leopard killed a 5-year-old boy in Uttarakhand.,0.98,single_incident,,NDTV,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,,extraction_failed(page_fetch_failed after resolved_via_decode)
"Leopard kills man in Pauri, 2nd fatal attack in U’khand in 3 days - The Times of India",2025-06-03,Uttarakhand,Pauri,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,"Leopard killed a man in Pauri, marking the second fatal attack in three days in Uttarakhand.",0.98,single_incident,,The Times of India,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Dehradun: A 55-year-old man was mauled to death by a leopard in Uttarakhand's Pauri district on Tuesday morning, marking the second fatal leopard attack in the state within three days.
Victim Puran Singh of Siroli village in Ekeshwar block had gone to the market on Monday evening but did not return till late in the night. His family informed local authorities and a search was initiated. Singh's body was found the next morning in a nearby forested area, with forest officials confirming that it was a leopard attack.
""This is the first leopard attack in the district in 10 months. We have deployed cages, trap cameras and tranquilisation teams. Patrolling has been intensified, and locals have been advised to remain vigilant,"" said divisional forest officer Swapnil Anirudh.
Monday's incident follows closely on the heels of another fatal leopard attack on Saturday night in Bhujiyaghat, located in Manora range of Nainital Forest Division, where a 70-year-old woman was killed. Pushpa Devi of Mora village stepped outside her home around 10.30 pm when a prowling leopard attacked her and tried to drag her into the nearby forest. 
Her screams alerted family members and neighbours, who rushed out and raised an alarm, prompting the leopard to release her and flee. Devi, who suffered severe injuries, was declared dead on arrival at Sushila Tiwari Hospital in Haldwani.
In another instance of escalating human-wildlife conflict in the state, a leopard snatched and killed a four-year-old boy from his mother's arms on May 3 in Mana Kabhra village, Bageshwar district. 
In April, Jogiyadi village in Garampani area of Betalghat block reported repeated sightings of a prowling leopard that killed several domestic animals over a month, sparking fear among residents and disrupting daily life. Earlier in January, a woman collecting fodder was seriously injured in a leopard attack in Bhelunta village, Tehri district.
In light of the growing threat, the state govt has issued safety advisories, urging residents to avoid venturing alone in forested areas, travel in groups and ensure adequate lighting around homes and livestock enclosures.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 2143 chars)"
Leopard kills woman grazing goats in Pauri Garhwal - The Times of India,2025-06-22,Uttarakhand,Pauri,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,Leopard killed a woman grazing goats in Pauri Garhwal.,0.98,single_incident,,The Times of India,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Dehradun: A leopard mauled a 35-year-old woman to death while she was grazing goats in her fields near forests after the predator ambushed her from behind bushes at Halsi village in Pauri Garhwal's Lansdowne forest division, Dwarikhal block, on Sunday evening. This was the third fatal leopard attack in the region within a month despite intensified patrolling and other mitigation measures by forest officials. 
Former gram panchayat of Jawad, Rajesh Miya, said Lata Devi screamed for help when the leopard attacked her but villagers were unable to save her. Forest and district administration officials reached the location soon after the incident to assist the victim's family. Villagers from nearby areas such as Banali, Kandakhal, Bistana, Jawar, and Birmoli demanded that forest officials kill the leopard, fearing it could attack others in the vicinity. 
Divisional forest officer (DFO) of Lansdowne, Aakash Gangwar, who met the family along with frontline staff, said the ex-gratia compensation process for the victim's family had begun. ""Camera traps and cages are being installed, and patrolling has increased to prevent further incidents,"" he added. 
Gangwar said Halsi village is surrounded by dense forests and bushes like Lantana camara, providing ideal cover for predators. He added, ""Only three families reside in that area, making isolated residents especially vulnerable to attacks, particularly during rains."" 
Leopard attacks have sharply risen in Uttarakhand, particularly in districts like Pauri, Almora, and Rudraprayag. Experts attribute this increasing conflict to shrinking habitats, reduced wild prey availability, and villagers regularly venturing into forests for livelihood activities. Over two dozen people have died in wildlife attacks across Uttarakhand this year, according to preliminary forest department data.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1846 chars)"
Leopard kills 7-year-old girl in Uttarakhand’s Almora | Hindustan Times - Hindustan Times,2020-09-20,Uttarakhand,Almora,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,"Leopard killed a 7-year-old girl in Almora, Uttarakhand.",0.98,single_incident,,Hindustan Times,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Leopard kills 7-year-old girl in Uttarakhand’s Almora
Children, who were playing with her, raised an alarm and informed local villagers about the incident
A girl (7) was mauled to death by a leopard when she was playing near her house in Uttarakhand’s Almora district, said forest officials.
The incident occurred on Saturday evening in a village that falls under the jurisdiction of Bhikiasain nagar panchayat.
Mohan Ram Arya, forest range officer, Bhikiasain, said, “The girl’s body has been recovered from a nearby bush of the village following a search operation. A cage is being installed to catch the leopard.”
