"Woman injured in bear attack in Tral, hospitalised - Kashmir News Observer",2026-09-11,Jammu Kashmir,,Asiatic Black Bear,Human Injury,0.0,1.0,0.0,Woman injured in bear attack and hospitalized.,0.98,single_incident,,Kashmir News Observer,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirAFBVV95cUxNb3hNMmphRjBaLUZLcWJScEFXeDltNmRWMDU5LUpGQTh4cU1aNXp4OFFSZGFfSnlCN2hwMURCOEM1RXV4R2Fuc1hxZEtYLXI1X1V5cXdac1hjcFNWTGdtSjhKNVV3MGM2UWZkakk2MVZqeWxfMmZ5QnZfUUhTTXJJQWM2b1dtX09yRzIzT3pFYXV6RHMwOVg1Mk9qWm1MejZwZENPZVhhUmxiSkhH?oc=5,,,"Srinagar, Sep 11 (KNO): A woman was injured after being attacked by a bear in the Handoora area of Tral in south Kashmir’s Pulwama district on Friday. An official told the news agency—Kashmir News Observer (KNO) that the woman was attacked by the wild animal in Handoora, leaving her injured. He said that she was soon shifted to Sub-District Hospital (SDH) Tral for treatment and was later identified as Hajra Begum, wife of Ghulam Ahmad Khan and a resident of Handoora. Meanwhile, locals have urged the Wildlife Department to take immediate preventive measures amid increased bear movement in the area.—(KNO)","success(newspaper3k, resolved_via_decode, 610 chars)"
Two injured in separate bear attacks in J&K's Banihal - Greater Kashmir,2021-07-04,Jammu Kashmir,,Asiatic Black Bear,Human Injury,0.0,2.0,0.0,Two people injured in separate bear attacks.,0.98,single_incident,,Greater Kashmir,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Banihal , July 4 : Two persons including a woman were injured in two separate bear attacks in Banihal area of Ramban district on Sunday.
Both the injured have been shifted to Emergency Hospital Banihal from where the man was referred to GMC Anantnag in view of his critical injures in the attack.
Officials told Greater Kashmir that the first incident took place in the Chapnari Guddar area of ​​Banihal on Sunday noon when, Wazeera Begum, a local woman walking near her house was attacked by a wild bear that appeared from nearby bushes.
The woman received injuries but was rescued by nearby villagers.
She was shifted to Emergency Hospital for treatment.
In the second attack, a nomadic Bakarwal was also attacked and injured seriously by a wild bear Sunday afternoon when he was grazing his sheep and goats in upper reaches of Kharpora Banihal.
The injured Bakarwal was identified as Mohammad Sharief son of Dawood Bakarwal, a resident of Kothi Jagir in Tehsil and district Ramban.
Volunteers from Banihal Volunteers group rushed the critically injured Bakarwal to Banihal Hospital from where he was shifted to Government Medical College Anantnag in view of his critical condition.
In-charge Wildlife Control Room Banihal Najamu Din Nayak told Greater Kashmir that after the two incidents of wild attacks, Wildlife teams from Banihal and Khari were dispatched to Chapnari and Kharpora upper reaches to drive wild beasts away from the area to avoid more wild and human confrontation.
He said compensation cases from wildlife department in favour of both wild animal attack victims are being prepared.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1602 chars)"
Jackal Leaves Three Persons Injured - Kashmir Life,2021-02-01,Jammu Kashmir,,Jackal,Human Injury,0.0,3.0,0.0,Three persons injured in jackal attack.,0.98,single_incident,,Kashmir Life,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTE4xZmVQUDVZRmo5Zy1YekZ6MERTWk1JU1lBNzl3N2RsRENSRmVQZHhuSTVPc0pXQlMwaWM0bnVMQTJvb1hKTWEzWm81eWRjdzYtM0RPTjAwcS1jTk5ySjZRcndDZlBmZl9DWFozR1lBVmctV25VY0E?oc=5,,,"SRINAGAR: Three persons were injured after a jackal attacked them in broad daylight by entering a residential house in Haril area of north Kashmir’s Kupwara district.

