Srinagar- A 28-year-old shepherd from Udhampur district was killed after being attacked by a bear in the Kharpath Larnoo forest area of Kokernag in South Kashmir’s Anantnag district on Wednesday.

ADVERTISEMENT

An official said the victim has been identified as Sadam Hussain Koshi, son of Ab Wahid Koshi, a resident of Majalta, Udhampur.

He was herding sheep when the wild animal attacked him around 3 PM, resulting in his on-spot death, reported news agency JKNS.

Officials said that the body was shifted to PHC Larnoo, where doctors declared him brought dead. After completion of medico-legal formalities, the body was handed over to his family for last rites.

Cognizance of the incident has been taken and further investigation started.","success(newspaper3k, resolved_via_decode, 768 chars)"
