The Chenab Times News Desk","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 2308 chars)"
Leopard attack leaves 16 sheep dead in Budgam - Rising Kashmir,2026-09-10,Kashmir,,Leopard,Livestock Attack,16.0,0.0,0.0,Leopard attack resulted in 16 sheep dead in Budgam.,0.98,single_incident,,Rising Kashmir,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxOaFcxU0VVdHgyd0I4cjNNXzkwS3FoMllRLWFOOWxlRFhLR1Rqcm1fQkExS2VESkRkbF9SV2dDS01fUENienY1RG1CdDdmOUxZbU11TlFxSGZGYUpaX05GR0dyaEV0UVRkZ0xQNm9qYkZ5R0k4TmxxdXY0VWlJaUU2MWdQMnlWWFVnWGJIRjlkNUo4bG1xM0RuTnJIaXdlVmhjSlZHUHUzR0w1MFN2M29uUQ?oc=5,,,"Budgam, Sep10: Sixteen sheep were killed and 17 others injured after a leopard attacked a flock in the Badipora area of Chadoora Tehsil in central Kashmir’s Budgam district during the intervening night of Wednesday and Thursday.
According to officials, the incident occurred when the leopard entered the  and attacked the flock, leaving several sheep dead and others injured.
Bashir Ahmad, Block Officer, Wildlife Control Budgam, said that a team from the Wildlife Department visited the spot after receiving information about the attack.
“We have visited the spot where the leopard attack took place. We have also installed two cages at the spot to capture the leopard alive,” Bashir Ahmad said.
He said that the department has launched a search operation in the area to trace and capture the animal.
“People should contact the Wildlife Department immediately if they spot the leopard anywhere in the district so that such incidents can be prevented,” he said.
The incident has caused concern among residents, particularly livestock owners, who have urged the authorities to take necessary measures to capture the leopard and prevent further attacks.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1151 chars)"
Jammu Kashmir: 15-Year-Old Injured in Leopard Attack - Kashmir Life,2026-01-16,Kashmir,,Leopard,Human Injury,0.0,1.0,0.0,15-year-old injured in leopard attack in Jammu Kashmir.,0.98,single_incident,,Kashmir Life,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiwFBVV95cUxOS0c0ampHdEtRMXoya2Z4Si1ja0JPVUtfZWI4QTFVV2s5eDVnOG0zME15M3FWZHVvYWZJMXQ1c3JnOGc1cXhhV1FjMVlZUHd6dWVqQ2FZS2NBb0g2UTZkeHo1UjNYQlUzU1BxejBlUnZ6QlVkVnBQUnM1TnRVNnJsenZBbFFDX29VdmFZ?oc=5,,,"SRINAGAR: A 15-year-old boy was injured in a leopard attack in a remote area of Rajouri district in Jammu and Kashmir on Thursday evening.

They said that the incident occurred in the evening hours at Panchayat Dodasan Balla (Remote), Ward No. 2, Gurah, when a leopard attacked a 15-year-old boy.

The injured boy was immediately rushed to the Community Health Centre (CHC) Thannamandi, where he was admitted for medical treatment. His condition was stated to be stable.

