The villagers said that it is the second such incident in the area within a month and it has created an atmosphere of fear among the residents.
They alleged that on Monday evening too, a leopard had attempted to attack Dev Singh Adhikari’s wife.
Champawat District Magistrate Manish Kumar said the forest department team is taking necessary action. In November, a leopard had killed a man in Kotla area of Barakot.
Chief Minister Pushkar Singh Dhami, who represents the Champawat assembly constituency, expressed grief over the incident and directed officials to provide assistance to the family of the deceased. He also directed the forest department to take all necessary steps in the area. PTI DPT NB NB
(This story has not been edited by News18 staff and is published from a syndicated news agency feed - PTI)","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1590 chars)"
Uttarakhand: Leopard responsible for death of 3 children killed in Tehri Garhwal | Hindustan Times - Hindustan Times,2024-11-27,Uttarakhand,,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,3.0,Leopard responsible for deaths of 3 children.,0.98,single_incident,,Hindustan Times,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Uttarakhand: Leopard responsible for death of 3 children killed in Tehri Garhwal
Shooters successfully neutralised the man-eater leopard as the big cat had killed three children in the last four months, officials said
A leopard responsible for the death of three children in Uttarakhand’s Tehri Garhwal region was killed by shooters of the state forest department on Tuesday evening, forest officials said.
“Our shooters successfully neutralised the man-eater leopard. The big cat had killed three children in the last four months. It was a female and seven years old. Several villages in the Bhilangana block were living in fear for the past few months. A postmortem of the leopard will be carried out before the carcass is burned by our officials”, Bhilangana range officer Ashish Nautiyal said.
Also Read: Maharashtra polls: Locals urge politicos to prioritise human-leopard conflict in Junnar
The female leopard is approximately seven years old, according to officials.
On October 19, the leopard was responsible for the death of a 13-year-old girl in Kot Maher village of the same block.
Following the last incident on October 19, Tehri district magistrate Mayur Dixit had declared a three-day holiday in the Bhaud village, Purwal village primary school, Anthwal village primary and high school as well as Anganwadi centres to ensure the safety of school students.
Half-yearly examinations in these schools were postponed.
The other two deaths took place on September 29 and July 22 respectively.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1501 chars)"
Leopard kills 3rd woman in week in Nainital - The Times of India,2026-01-12,Uttarakhand,Nainital,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,Leopard kills third woman in Nainital in a week.,0.98,single_incident,,The Times of India,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"NAINITAL: A 35-year-old woman was mauled to death by a suspected leopard while collecting firewood near her home in Nainital's Dhari block on Jan 2, in the third such fatal attack in the area within a week. The incident triggered panic and protests in Khutiyakhal village, with residents demanding immediate action against the predator and criticising the forest department's inaction.
Ganga Devi had gone to the nearby forest in the morning for daily chores when the leopard attacked her, dragged her away and killed her. Villagers launched a search operation after hearing her screams and later recovered her mutilated body nearly 2km away from the village.
Police took the body for post-mortem while forest department officials reached the site and issued advisories asking villagers to avoid forested areas during early morning and evening hours. Patrolling has also been stepped up in the region.
Residents blamed the forest department for failing to act despite repeated alerts about leopard sightings. ""We are living in constant fear. People cannot even go out to gather fodder or firewood. 
How many more lives will be lost before something is done? The leopard should be shot immediately,"" said a resident.
This was the third fatal leopard attack reported in the area in less than a week. On Dec 26, a woman named Hema was killed by a leopard in Dini Talli village of Dhari block. On Dec 30, another woman was mauled to death in Chamoli village of Khansyu while collecting firewood and fodder.
With three deaths in quick succession, public anger has grown. Nainital divisional forest officer Aakash Gangwar, told TOI that officials are monitoring the area and more steps are being taken to track the animal. ""We had already installed cages and camera traps, but the animal has not been spotted. Now, we are adding more cages and building a machan to observe its movements. We are considering capture or tranquilisation,"" he said.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1938 chars)"
Uttarakhand: Leopard mauls 4-year-old girl to death in Pauri - News18,2025-09-13,Uttarakhand,Pauri,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,Leopard mauls four-year-old girl to death in Pauri.,0.98,single_incident,,News18,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Uttarakhand: Leopard mauls 4-year-old girl to death in Pauri
Kotdwar, Sept 13 (PTI) A four-year-old girl was mauled to death by a leopard in the Chaubattakhal area of Pauri district in Uttarakhand, a forest official said on Saturday.
Riya was playing on the balcony of her house on Friday evening when the leopard pounced upon her and dragged her away, the official said.
Her mother raised an alarm and ran after the leopard, which left the child in a field about 50 metres from the house and ran away. By the time the family members reached the spot, the child was dead, the forest conservator of Garhwal Circle, Akash Verma, said.
As soon as the information was received, teams from the administration, forest department and health department reached the spot.
The deceased was the youngest of two sisters. The family was preparing to celebrate her birthday on September 17, for which her father Jitendra Singh Rawat came to the village from Mumbai.
A forest department team has been deployed in the area where two cages have been installed to capture the big cat, Verma said, adding that three more cages are being installed.
The last rites of the girl were not performed till Saturday evening, as the family insisted on issuing an order to kill the leopard, before Lansdowne Divisional Forest Officer Jeevan Mohan Degade convinced them about the efforts being made to capture the animal.
Locals claimed that leopards are often seen in the area, insisting that the government must take special steps to ensure people’s safety. PTI COR ALM ARI
(This story has not been edited by News18 staff and is published from a syndicated news agency feed - PTI)","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1652 chars)"
"Leopard attacks camping site in Champawat, injures man from Sikkim - The Times of India",2026-03-26,Uttarakhand,,Leopard,Human Injury,0.0,1.0,0.0,Leopard injured a man at a camping site.,0.98,single_incident,,The Times of India,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Pithoragarh: A 45-year-old man from Sikkim sustained injuries on his face and arms after a leopard attacked him inside a camping site at Pancheswar in Lohaghat block of Champawat district on Tuesday evening, forest officials said Wednesday.
Tourist guide Mahesh Bhatt said that a leopard had entered the campsite and damaged tents earlier in the day. The animal had also attempted to approach a group gathered here but went into hiding upon seeing a crowd, he added.
Later, the leopard attacked Ian Christopher, who was camping on the banks of Kali river. He was initially taken to Lohaghat Hospital and later referred to district hospital where doctor Viraj Rathi said his condition is stable.
""Forest department teams reached the spot and launched a search operation after being informed that the leopard had retreated into the forest,"" said Lohaghat ranger Narayan Pandey. ""However, no trace of the animal was found.""
This is the second leopard attack in the area in three days. On Sunday, Geeta Devi, 28, was injured in a similar attack at Dhauni Silling. Officials have installed four camera traps and a cage at Dhauni Silling and plan to install three more cages at Pancheswar.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1183 chars)"
Man attacked by leopard in Sattari dies of injuries - The Times of India,2026-02-18,,,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,Man died from injuries after leopard attack.,0.98,single_incident,,The Times of India,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Valpoi:
 A 59-year-old resident of Charavane who was attacked by a leopard between Thane and Charavane in Sattari taluka on Friday evening succumbed to his injuries on Tuesday.
Yashwant Gawas, who works as a mechanic at the state police headquarters, was returning home from duty on his scooter when he was attacked by a wild animal.
A girl from his village, whom he offered a lift to, escaped with minor injuries. According to villagers, the sudden attack by the leopard caused both to lose balance and fall off the scooter. Locals rushed to their rescue, and both were taken to the Valpoi community health centre.
The girl was discharged the same day, but Gawas, having sustained a major head injury, was transferred to the GMC. He, however, succumbed to his injuries late Monday evening.
The death has triggered anger and fear across the rural belt of Sattari. Residents say the stretch of road where the attack occurred is frequented by wild animals at night.
In the past, locals have reported repeated sightings of leopards roaming near human settlements and allegedly attacking domestic animals such as dogs and calves.
Residents have expressed serious concerns about the safety of children, elderly persons, and livestock. They have urged the forest department to intensify patrolling especially at night, install surveillance systems in the area and take immediate preventive measures to prevent any further loss of life.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1429 chars)"
Leopard kills 14 goats in Gethiya Sanatorium area - Pioneer Edge,2026-06-30,,,Leopard,Livestock Attack,14.0,0.0,0.0,Leopard killed livestock in Gethiya Sanatorium area.,0.98,single_incident,,Pioneer Edge,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE9Va1I4U1dRblN4RTFkME5lRWgyeFNhSnZNWHViVWstSlVfRGxhUUplV002ZGJ5bElqcVJBcWJUSWQ5TzZ0S3NIYkQtNXhKRnNLQUJnVk9fLUhkbk1qQ2xYN0ctd3VsWW8zY2F0akpfVDhpODIwbVVBUVp2QVBJUQ?oc=5,,,"PIONEER EDGE NEWS SERVICE/ Nainital
In an incident that triggered concerns among the villagers, a leopard sneaked into the goat pen and killed 14 goats. The incident happened late in the night at Gethiya Sanatorium near Nainital.
Prakash Chandra, a resident of Gethiya, supports his family by rearing goats. When he went to feed the goats in the morning, he was shocked having found all his goats dead. He further said that while 12 goats were found dead inside the enclosure, the rest two had been dragged away by the leopard. “With all the goats dead, I do not know how we will carry on,” he said.
Queried over the incident, the range officer of Nainital Forest Division, Nitin Pant said that upon receiving the information, the forest inspector Rajendra Karayat and beat officer Hira Giri had gone to the spot and investigated. “Necessary action will be taken after we receive the report. The man who lost all his goats might be compensated as per the rules,” he added.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 972 chars)"
Uttarakhand: 4-year-old girl killed in leopard attack - The Times of India,2018-09-04,Uttarakhand,,Leopard,Human Death,0.0,0.0,1.0,A 4-year-old girl was killed in a leopard attack.,0.98,single_incident,,The Times of India,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"In a tragic case, a 4-year-old girl was killed after a leopard attacks her at Garud Tehsil in Bageshwar district,Uttarakhand. The incident happened during Janmashtami when her family members were busy preparing for the festival. Around 8.30 in the evening, the leopard picks up the girl identified as Jyoti from outside her home. After hearing the girl’s screams, family members started searching for her but are unable to trace her. Later with the help of forest officials, they found her body 100 meters away from home.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 521 chars)"
2 forest guards injured while rescuing leopard in Pauri - The Times of India,2026-08-27,Uttarakhand,,Leopard,Human Injury,0.0,2.0,0.0,Forest guards were injured while rescuing a leopard.,0.98,single_incident,,The Times of India,https://news.google.?oc=5,,,"Dehradun: Two forest guards sustained injuries to their arms and neck after a partially sedated leopard attacked them during a rescue operation in Uttarakhand’s Pauri district around 8.30am on Thursday.
The forest officials had reached Maso village after receiving information that a leopard was trapped inside a chicken coop. The team administered a tranquiliser to safely extract the big cat, however, the rescue attempt got complicated as villagers gathered around the coop, obstructing smooth operation.
“Forest personnel spent nearly 30 minutes convincing the anxious crowd to step back to avoid any mishaps. That delay proved critical. By the time the rescue team entered the enclosure to secure the animal, the sedative began to wear off, allowing the leopard to regain consciousness and strike,” said Mahatim Yadav, divisional forest officer, Pauri.
Both injured forest guards were taken to Pauri district govt hospital, where they received stitches for injuries on their arms. One of them also suffered claw marks on his neck. They were subsequently discharged in a stable condition.
Officials said the team had to wait about four hours, in accordance with standard wildlife medical protocols, before administering a second dose of the sedative to the animal. The leopard was recaptured later in the afternoon.
The leopard is undergoing a medical examination after which forest officials will decide whether to release it into the wild or relocate it to a rescue centre. Residents remain concerned as a leopard was trapped in the same chicken coop three months ago. Officials emphasised that local safety and animal welfare will guide their final decision.","success(trafilatura, resolved_via_decode, 1665 chars)"
Bear mauls man in Shopian’s apple orchard - Asian Mail,2026-09-11,Jammu & Kashmir,,Asiatic Black Bear,Human Injury,0.0,1.0,0.0,A man was mauled by a bear in an apple orchard.,0.98,single_incident,,Asian Mail,https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifkFVX3lxTE5GVFlLcHFpaktrNE8zRGQ3eWpaWEpvaXdHSGRnSC1JWk9NQkNyeVRDbGJlX1RxYldnc2RWaGFiN1ZELVdPdWtVVTFYNEhqTFh1d1RLQ01sZjl5UmhkYXJFWDlBNTVTZFBod09mVnVxVHVMU1ZPdlBDVDBUcnJMQQ?oc=5,,,"Srinagar, Sep 11: A 40-year-old man was injured after being attacked by a wild bear in an apple orchard in the Sedow area of Shopian district on Friday.

An official told the news agency—Kashmir News Observer (KNO) that the man was attacked by the wild animal in the apple orchard at Sedow, Shopian.

He said the man was shifted to Sub-District Hospital (SDH) Shopian for treatment. He was identified as Sadiq Ahmad Thokar (40), son of Abdul Rahman, a resident of Sedow.

Meanwhile, cognisance of the incident has been taken.—(KNO)","success(newspaper3k, resolved_via_decode, 531 chars)"
